  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose a strategy that leverages convex optimization and local search for a structured, mathematically sound solution. The problem is convex in h, enabling global optima via CVXPY, with SLSQP for local refinement. This approach avoids stochastic pitfalls while ensuring feasibility.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe define h \u2208 [0,1]^n s.t. sum(h) = n/2. The overlap integral for shift k is sum(h_i (1 - h_{i+k})). We minimize the maximum overlap across all k.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Use CVXPY to set up and solve the convex problem.\nb) Validate and refine the solution with SLSQP.\nc) Handle feasibility and constraints explicitly.\n\n4. Search choices\nWe initialize from initial_h and solve the convex problem exactly. This deterministic approach avoids local optima and ensures recovery.\n\n5. Compute budget\nExpected runtime: 600s maximum. CVXPY's quick, deterministic, with SLSQP for refinement. Monitoring ensures completion within budget.\n\n6. Validation\nCheck each solution for feasibility (sum, bounds). Refine and evaluate overlap with the original metric.\n\nThe code will:\n\n1. Use CVXPY to set up and solve the convex program.\n2. Use SLSQP for fine-tuning near the optimal solution.\n3. Ensure all constraints are met throughout.",
